  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \n\nSome river valley fog is possible this morning, but high level clouds\nwill limit overall fog development. \n\nA cut off low has developed along the Atlantic Coast, with the Ohio \nValley on the far western periphery of this low. The synotpic \npattern will continue to favor a period of northeasterly flow, \nushering in a drier air mass along with seasonably cooler air. This \nwill persist the remainder of this weekend and linger into early next\nweek.\n\nBy late Monday, the upper low is absorbed back into the mean H5 flow\nand carried off to the northeast. This shift will result in return \nflow developing across the Ohio Valley come Tuesday. A subtle warming\ntrend will then ensue as we progress through the rest of the work \nweek, and the pattern looks to become more unsettled as rain chances \nreturn.",
